# Diagnostics' page changes: A on "start?" shows the first step at once
# (v0.3.2: about 80 frames later, while the log file was made), and each
# page's title comes in with its lines, in the same frame (it came about 40
# frames before them), every frame hashed from A until the cart page is up
# (its later lines show the build). The save memory page shows "reading the
# 128 KB save chip twice..." while it reads (it showed the previous page's
# lines, then a blank body), and the timings page holds no half-scrolled
# row under its title.
# Diagnostics from L+R+SELECT held at power-on (B17 moves it to Info), A
# once its first page is up and those keys are let go
-k 1:L+R+SELECT
-w "screen ready: diag-start"
-k 60:-
-k @40:A -k @44:-
-H @40:@47
-w "diag: reading the 128 KB save chip twice"
-s @20:save-memory.png
-w "diag: PSRAM 4018"
-s @1:timings.png
